      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright 1999 Elsevier Science B.V.",
        "AbstractText": "The development of thermal allodynia in relationship to sodium channel augmentation in dorsal root ganglia (DRGs) was studied in albino rats. Paw withdrawal latencies were measured hourly following complete Freund's adjuvant (CFA) injections. Sodium channels were demonstrated with immunocytochemistry. Sustained minimum latencies were attained between 10 and 12 h post-injection. Sodium channel labeling began to increase at 23 h post-injection and reached maximum levels by 24 h. Thermal hypersensitivity is thus established 12 h before sodium channel augmentation can be demonstrated."
      },
